A JSON object with a missing comma, as in a half-edited file, still lists every key: the parser
holds the keys before the gap in an `ERROR` node inside the object, which are read as the
object's own.
== args
input/broken.json
== file input/broken.json
{
  "name": "demo",
  "version": "1.0.0"
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {}
}
== stdout
input/broken.json (6 lines)
[L2-L2] name: "demo"
[L3-L3] version: "1.0.0"
[L4-L4] private: true
[L5-L5] scripts
== stderr
== exit 0
